  "question": "1) Background / Context  \nUdiddit is a social news aggregation platform designed for web content rating and discussion. Currently, the system employs a Postgres database schema to manage user-generated content, including forum posts, discussions, and votes. However, the existing schema is considered risky and unreliable, necessitating improvements for data integrity and system robustness.\n\n2) Objectives  \n- Enhance the reliability and security of the database schema for Udiddit.\n- Ensure seamless content creation and interaction among users.\n- Support scalable user activities including posting, voting, and commenting.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users  \n- Registered Users: Individuals who create posts, engage in discussions, and vote on content.\n- Developers: Responsible for maintaining and upgrading the database schema and ensuring system integrity.\n- Administrators: Oversee user management and general platform operations.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions  \n- User Registration: Allow users to register with unique usernames, up to 25 characters, and ensure active user management.\n- Content Posting: Enable users to create posts under various topics, with titles up to 100 characters. Posts can include URLs (up to 2000 characters) or text content.\n- Commenting System: Users can add comments to posts, as well as reply to existing comments (nested commenting).\n- Voting Mechanism: Implement a voting system allowing users to upvote or downvote posts, with each vote represented as 1 (upvote) or -1 (downvote).\n- Topic Management: Facilitate the creation and management of topics, allowing description fields up to 500 characters.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions  \n- Data Integrity: Implement constraints to ensure the accuracy and completeness of data entries.\n- Performance: Optimize the database to handle a large volume of concurrent operations efficiently.\n- Security: Enforce secure operations such as reliable logins and safe handling of user-generated content to prevent misuse and ensure data protection.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0190\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(25) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `is_active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `username` (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `topics` (\n  `topic_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `topic_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`topic_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `topic_name` (`topic_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `posts` (\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `topic_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(2000) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`post_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `topic_id` (`topic_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`topic_id`) REFERENCES `topics` (`topic_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  KEY `post_id` (`post_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `parent_comment_id` (`parent_comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`post_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`comment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `votes` (\n  `vote_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vote_value` tinyint(4) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`vote_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `post_user_unique` (`post_id`,`user_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`post_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
